                    The setting only applies to 3PCC server environments.
                    Not used for BLA.
                    '0' Barge in is disabled for the shared line
                    '1' Barge in is enabled for the shared line (default)"
                    ::= { endptSIP 165 }

endptENABLESIPURIHOSTVALIDATION  OBJECT-TYPE
                    SYNTAX      INTEGER
                    MAX-ACCESS  read-only
                    STATUS      current
                    DESCRIPTION "Allows accepting SIP URI with unrecognized host part in INVITE message.
                    Ranges 0 - 1 (default)."
                    ::= { endptSIP 166 }

endptCALLFWDCHAINORDER  OBJECT-TYPE
                    SYNTAX      INTEGER
                    MAX-ACCESS  read-only
                    STATUS      current
                    DESCRIPTION "Forwarded by details are shown for incoming calls that have been forwarded by another user.
                    CALLFWD_CHAIN_ORDER specifies which user information is displayed on an incoming call if there have been multiple forwards before being received as an incoming call.
                    '0' (Default) - the first CFWD party is displayed
                    '1' - the last CFWD party is displayed"
                    ::= { endptSIP 167 }

endptSHAREDLINE1INCOMINGCALLINDICATIONDEFAULT  OBJECT-TYPE
                    SYNTAX      INTEGER
                    MAX-ACCESS  read-only
                    STATUS      current
                    DESCRIPTION "Specifies how a Shared Call Appearance Line should behave when receiving an incoming call.
                    This parameter is applicable for SCA, BLA and BCA.
                    This is administrator part of the setting.
                    Indication Value can be:
                    0 - None
                    1 - Audible
                    2 - Visual
                    3 - Both (Default)
                    4 - None Forced
                    5 - Audible Forced
                    6 - Visual Forced
                    7 - Both Forced
                    Values <= 3 allow user to modify the setting in the User Menu.
                    This setting does not apply to a primary line which is shared."
                    ::= { endptSIP 168 }

